---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  title="The # became a portal — why SoloMD has a new logo"
  description="The thinking behind SoloMD's new orange # Portal: why we kept the Markdown symbol, removed the MD letters, drew it from geometry, and gave documents their own icon."
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="container blog-article">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blog/">Blog</a> / <span>A new face for SoloMD</span>
      </nav>
      <time>2026-08-02</time>
      <h1>The # became a portal.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        SoloMD 4.11.3 has a new logo. We kept the one character that says
        Markdown without explanation, removed the generic letters around it,
        and opened a small portal at its center.
      </p>

      <div class="brand-stage" aria-label="SoloMD's new orange hash portal logo">
        <img src="/favicon.svg?v=4.11.4" alt="SoloMD # Portal logo" width="232" height="232" />
        <div>
          <span>THE NEW MARK</span>
          <strong># Portal</strong>
          <p>Markdown structure outside. An opening for ideas, files and agents inside.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What the old mark got right</h2>
      <p>
        The original <code>#MD</code> mark was direct. It told you what the app
        opened before you knew its name, and the orange hash gave SoloMD a
        recognizable color from day one. That clarity was worth keeping.
      </p>
      <p>
        But it was still a word set in a font. At dock size, the letters merged
        into a white bar. In a browser tab they disappeared. And <code>MD</code>
        described a file extension more than a product that had grown into a
        workspace for notes, diagrams, local AI and publishing.
      </p>

      <div class="before-after">
        <div class="before-after__old" aria-label="Old SoloMD word mark">
          <span><b>#</b>MD</span>
          <small>BEFORE · a label</small>
        </div>
        <div class="before-after__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="before-after__new">
          <img src="/favicon.svg?v=4.11.4" alt="New SoloMD logo" width="116" height="116" />
          <small>NOW · a symbol</small>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Why a portal?</h2>
      <p>
        A hash is Markdown's most familiar piece of structure: one character
        turns a line into a heading and gives a document shape. We redrew that
        hash from four solid geometric strokes, then cut a warm-paper diamond
        into the center. The diamond reads as a cursor, a spark, a vault opening
        or a doorway depending on its size. All four interpretations belong in
        SoloMD.
      </p>
      <p>
        The result still says “Markdown” at a glance, but it also points forward.
        SoloMD is where plain files open into something larger: a linked vault,
        a publishable document, a diagram, or a workspace an agent can help with.
        The logo does not abandon the file. It shows the opening inside it.
      </p>

      <h2>Drawn, not typed</h2>
      <p>
        Every visible part of the mark is original geometry. There is no logo
        font and no borrowed glyph. That gives us a shape we can own, tune and
        reproduce consistently from a 16-pixel browser tab to a 1024-pixel store
        listing. The graphite square keeps the app grounded; the same SoloMD
        orange keeps continuity with every previous release.
      </p>

      <h2>One identity, two jobs</h2>
      <p>
        The app icon and a Markdown file should feel related without becoming
        indistinguishable. The app gets the dark # Portal: the tool and the
        doorway. Documents get a warm paper sheet, an orange folded corner and
        the Portal as a smaller seal, with two quiet text lines beneath it.
        Finder can now tell “open SoloMD” from “open this note” at a glance.
      </p>

      <div class="identity-pair">
        <div>
          <img src="/favicon.svg?v=4.11.4" alt="SoloMD app icon" width="128" height="128" />
          <strong>App</strong>
          <span>The portal</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src="/file-icon.svg" alt="SoloMD Markdown document icon" width="128" height="128" />
          <strong>Document</strong>
          <span>The page</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What changed, and what did not</h2>
      <p>
        The new identity now ships across macOS, Windows, Linux, iOS, Android,
        installers, store artwork, document associations and this website. What
        did not change is more important: SoloMD is still free, MIT-licensed,
        local-first, built around ordinary files, and orange in exactly the same
        slightly warm way.
      </p>
      <p>
        A good software logo should become boring in the best sense: easy to
        find, hard to mistake, and quiet enough to live beside your work every
        day. That is what this one is designed to do.
      </p>

      <p class="article-cta">
        The new mark ships in <a href="/whats-new/">SoloMD 4.11.3</a>.
        <a href="/#download">Download it here</a>.
      </p>

      <Giscus />
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BlogPosting',
  headline: 'The # became a portal — why SoloMD has a new logo',
  datePublished: '2026-08-02',
  dateModified: '2026-08-02',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'xiangdong li', url: 'https://github.com/zhitongblog' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'xiangdong li' },
  image: 'https://solomd.app/og-image.png',
  url: 'https://solomd.app/blog/v4-11-3-new-logo/',
  description: "The design thinking behind SoloMD's new orange # Portal logo and its matching document icon.",
  about: ['logo design', 'visual identity', 'Markdown', 'SoloMD'],
})} />

<style>
  .blog-article { max-width: 780px; padding: 40px 20px 80px; }
  .breadcrumbs { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .breadcrumbs a { color: inherit; }
  .blog-article > time { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .blog-article h1 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.6rem); line-height: 1.02; margin: 14px 0 22px; max-width: 11ch; }
  .blog-article h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 42px 0 12px; }
  .blog-article .lead { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .blog-article p { line-height: 1.78; margin: 14px 0; }
  .blog-article code { background: var(--bg-elev); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .brand-stage { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 38px; margin: 42px 0; padding: 42px; border-radius: 28px; background: #121110; color: #fff9ef; overflow: hidden; }
  .brand-stage img { width: 232px; height: 232px; border-radius: 48px; box-shadow: 0 24px 70px rgba(255,159,64,.24); }
  .brand-stage div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .brand-stage span { color: #ff9f40; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .16em; }
  .brand-stage strong { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2.15rem; margin: 7px 0; }
  .brand-stage p { color: #b9b2a6; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }
  .before-after { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 20px; margin: 34px 0; }
  .before-after > div:not(.before-after__arrow) { min-height: 180px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 18px; background: var(--bg-elev); }
  .before-after__old span { font: 700 48px/1 var(--font-mono); color: var(--text); }
  .before-after__old b { color: #ff9f40; }
  .before-after__new img { border-radius: 24px; }
  .before-after small { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .13em; }
  .before-after__arrow { color: #ff9f40; font-size: 25px; }
  .identity-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px; margin: 34px 0; }
  .identity-pair > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; padding: 28px; border-radius: 20px; background: var(--bg-elev); border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .identity-pair img { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .identity-pair strong { font-size: 14px; }
  .identity-pair span { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .article-cta { margin-top: 42px !important; padding: 22px 24px; border-left: 3px solid #ff9f40; background: var(--bg-elev); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .brand-stage { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; padding: 28px; }
    .brand-stage img { width: 152px; height: 152px; border-radius: 32px; }
    .before-after { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .before-after__arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); text-align: center; }
  }
</style>
